{{!-- Complimentary-access surface for /membership/.

     Comped members used to fall into partials/membership-already
     alongside paid members and were told "You're already a member"
     with no way to start paying. That is wrong for this cohort: a
     comped member has full access but no subscription, and 1,206 of
     them (legacy HubSpot migrants, Patreon imports, Substack imports,
     Donors) are people who in many cases *want* to pay us.

     So: name the complimentary access plainly, then show the same
     pricing cards everyone else sees. No new CSS — .pricing,
     .container and .already-member already exist, and the cards come
     from the shared membership-pricing partial. --}}
<section class="pricing pricing-comped-note">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="already-member">
      Your access to Mere&nbsp;Orthodoxy is currently complimentary — you're reading everything, and nothing is being charged.
      If you'd like to support the work, you can become a paying member below.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{{> "membership-pricing"}}
